# Copy to .env and uncomment what you want to change; `docker compose up -d --wait` picks it up.
# The values shown are the defaults baked into compose.yaml and tools/serve.sh.

# Weights: bartowski's imatrix GGUFs of Nanbeige4.3-33B. Q4_K_M (20.8 GB), Q5_K_M (25.1), Q6_K (29.0) or Q8_0 (35.2).
#QUANT=Q6_K
# Speculative decoding: draft+ngram (Nanbeige4.1-3B drafts for the 33B, plus n-gram lookups in the prompt), draft,
# ngram or none. All of them are lossless: the 33B checks every drafted token. The drafter speeds up one request
# by 70% but costs 15% throughput with 4 requests in flight; serve many parallel requests with SPEC=none.
#SPEC=draft+ngram
# Tokens the drafter proposes per step, and the drafter confidence below which it stops early.
#SPEC_DRAFT_MAX=4
#SPEC_DRAFT_P_MIN=0.6

# Context size llama-server allocates (native window: 524288). f16 KV costs about 208 KB per token,
# so 262144 tokens take about 54 GB. Slots share it.
#CONTEXT=262144
# Server slots. Raise for concurrent requests.
#PARALLEL=1
# Prompt-processing micro-batch. 2048 gives 12% faster prefill than llama.cpp's default of 512, same decode.
#UBATCH=2048

# Sampling from the model card's agentic preset; chat and reasoning: TEMP=0.6. Requests can override per call.
#TEMP=1.0
#TOP_P=0.95
#TOP_K=0
#MIN_P=0

#SERVED_NAME=nanbeige
#HOST=0.0.0.0
#PORT=8888
# Set to require a bearer token on the API.
#API_KEY=

#MODEL_ID=bartowski/Nanbeige_Nanbeige4.3-33B-GGUF
#MODEL_REVISION=9beb68421fdf7be095093a6888325fa2c83ddd38
# llama.cpp b11870 (74bca3950), the arm64 CUDA 13 image.
#LLAMA_CPP_IMAGE=ghcr.io/ggml-org/llama.cpp:server-cuda13@sha256:2ac42bff86574137dd69b1c8ad85330729d8292e1b4fac0639b67a722c4e9558

#MODEL_DIR=~/.cache/nanbeige
# Only needed if the model ever becomes gated.
#HF_TOKEN=
